# One closure body reads `this[target][name]` for many names, and the second read finds a getter two objects above the receiver. The stub that reads by key remembers the word that holds the accessor, under the key's cell and the
# receiver's structure, and forgets it with all that says absence as soon as an object on some way up changes: the getter defined anew, taken away, hidden in between, the way up relinked, the receiver given its own.
# RUN: run-in-shell
# CHECK: size of kept;color of kept;weight of kept;shade of kept;
# CHECK: a new getter, kept;color of kept;
# CHECK: a new getter, kept;undefined;weight of kept;
# CHECK: a new getter, kept;undefined;hidden in between;shade of kept;
# CHECK: undefined;undefined;hidden in between;from elsewhere, kept;
# CHECK: undefined;undefined;hidden in between;its own; undefined;undefined;hidden in between;from elsewhere, last;
# CHECK: the source prints the same
